<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.9.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01893</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.9.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>be9e7279-162a-42be-9cb1-28004955d73e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<section class="check-understanding"><exercise data-content-id="93136e8c-aab9-46b5-809e-92dca8685ecf" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Choose the standard form of the quadratic expression.</para>
        <para> \((x+4)(x-1)\)</para>
          <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(x^2-3x+4\)</para><para>\(-x^2+3x-4\)</para><para>\(x^2+3x-4\)</para><para>\(-x^2-3x+4\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(x^2+3x-4\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.9.3 and 7.9.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(x^2+3x-4\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="3dc098a3-f2cf-4a46-99c0-6e4ab2f5b443" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> \((2x-1)(3x-1)\) </para>
        <para>Multiple Choice:</para><para>\(6x^2+5x-1\)</para><para>\(6x^2-5x+1\)</para><para>\(-6x^2-5x+1\)</para><para>\(-6x^2+5x-1\)</para></problem><solution><para>Correct! \(6x^2-5x+1\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.9.3 and 7.9.4. </para><para>The correct answer is \(6x^2-5x+1\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="af11d46b-2aed-4e89-b6cc-5632958fb11a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Consider the expression \(8-6x+x^2\). </para>
      <para>Is the expression in standard form? </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! No. Even though it has \(x^2\) term, it does not start with the \(x^2\) term.</para><para>Try again. Revisit activities 7.9.3 and 7.9.4.</para><para>The correct answer is No. Even though it starts with a number and ends with an \(x^2\), it is not of the form \(ax^2+bx+c\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="d5826ad8-8703-41aa-96ee-3c02dd045b4a" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para> Is the expression equivalent to \((x-4)(x-2)\)? </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! Yes. Applying the distributive property gives \(x^2-2x-4x+8\) or \(x^2-6x+8\), which is equivalent to \(8-6x+x^2\).</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.9.2.</para><para>The correct answer is Yes. Applying the distributive property gives \(x^2-2x-4x+8\) or \(x^2-6x+8\), which is equivalent to \(8-6x+x^2\). </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="b4acb530-d810-4f25-95f7-c2739c0fe041" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>Find the standard form of the quadratic expression \((x-2)(x+8)\). Use the standard form to answer questions a, b, and c. 
          
          <para>What is the value of \(a\) in this expression \(ax^2+bx+c\)?</para>
          </para>
      </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(a\)=1</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.9.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \(a\)=1. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="6aee0d16-970b-4113-9c10-b99d81df4403" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para> What is the value of \(b\) in this expression \(ax^2+bx+c\)? </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(b\)=6 </para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.9.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \(b\)=6. </para></solution></exercise><exercise data-content-id="cabf4259-4429-448e-b6af-9c1bbdb4f4be" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>Enter your answer here:</para><para>What is the value of \(c\) in this expression \(ax^2+bx+c\)? </para>
        </problem><solution><para>Correct! \(c=-16\)</para><para>Try again. Revisit activity 7.9.2. </para><para>The correct answer is \(c=-16\). </para></solution></exercise></section></section>
